{"name":"Buckeye","hex":"#674834","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Buckeye","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A native or resident of the American states of Ohio or Arizona."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A number of places in the United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Buckeye"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ohio State Buckeyes","blocks":[{"text":"The Ohio State Buckeyes are the intercollegiate athletic teams that represent Ohio State University, located in Columbus, Ohio. The athletic programs are named after the colloquial term for people from the state of Ohio and after the state tree, the Ohio buckeye. The Buckeyes participate in the National Collegiate Athletic Association's (NCAA) Division I and the Big Ten Conference in most sports. The Ohio State women's ice hockey team competes in the Western Collegiate Hockey Association (WCHA). The school colors are scarlet and gray. The university's mascot is Brutus Buckeye. \"THE\" is the official trademark of the Ohio State University merchandise. Led by its football program, the Buckeyes have the largest overall sports endowment of any campus in North America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Ohio_State_Buckeyes_logo.svg/330px-Ohio_State_Buckeyes_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ohio_State_Buckeyes","wikidata":"Q2927468"},{"title":"Buckeye (candy)","blocks":[{"text":"Buckeyes are confections made from a peanut butter fudge partially dipped in chocolate to leave a circle of peanut butter visible. Buckeyes are similar to peanut butter balls, which are completely covered in chocolate. While similar to the more widely known Reese's cup, the buckeye has a higher ratio of peanut butter to chocolate and a smoother texture due to the use of powdered sugar to make the peanut butter into a fudge. Buckeye candies are also often stored in the fridge or freezer giving a snap to the chocolate coating."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Buckeyes_Peanut_Butter_Balls%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Buckeyes_Peanut_Butter_Balls%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buckeye_(candy)","wikidata":"Q4983108"},{"title":"Buckeye (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Buckeye is a historical fiction novel by Patrick Ryan. The book follows two couples from the fictional town of Bonhomie, Ohio from World War II to the end of the 20th century and the secrets which develop between them. It is Ryan's first full length novel for adults and received favorable reviews from critics."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f4/Buckeye_book_cover.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buckeye_(novel)","wikidata":"Q139505725"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Ohio_state_wordmark_2013.png/500px-Ohio_state_wordmark_2013.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Ohio_state_wordmark_2013.png/500px-Ohio_state_wordmark_2013.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOhio_state_wordmark_2013.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Ohio_State_%283335623823%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Ohio_State_%283335623823%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Ohio_State_%283335623823%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Ohio_State_%283335623823%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Buckeyes baseball players before a 2009 game","link":"